Concentrations of ions in $0.1 $\mathrm{M} potassium nitrate (KCl) is $=0.1 $\left(1\right.$ mole of $\mathrm{K}^{+}+1$ mole of $\left.\mathrm{Cl}^{-}\right)$
=0.1 $\times$2=0.2 $\mathrm{M}$Concentration of ions in $0.1 \mathrm{M}$ magnesium chloride $\left(\mathrm{MgCl}_{2}\right)$ is $=0.1 \left($1\right.$ mole of  \mathrm{Mg}^{2+}+$2$ moles of \left.\mathrm{Cl}^{-}\right)
=0.1 \times 3=0.3 \mathrm{M}

Concentration of ions in $0.1 $\mathrm{M} barium chloride \left(\mathrm{BaCl}_{2}\right) is $=0.1 $\left(1\right.$ mole of $\mathrm{Ba}^{2+}+2$ moles of $\left.\mathrm{Cl}^{-}\right)$
=0.1 $\times$3=0.3 $\mathrm{M}\therefore$ Order of concentration is
$0.1 \mathrm{M} \mathrm{Al}_{2}\left(\mathrm{SO}_{4}\right)_{3} \gt 0.1 \mathrm{M} \mathrm{KCl} \gt 0.1 \mathrm{MgCl}_{2}=0.1 \mathrm{M} \mathrm{BaCl}_{2}\because$ Osmotic pressure is colligative property and, it depends on concentration of ions.
