37635.sol:
Let 5 th observation be $x$.
Given mean $=7 \begin{aligned}$& \therefore 7=$\frac{6+7+8+10+x}{5}$\\
& \Rightarrow x=4
\end{aligned}

Now, Variance

$\begin{gathered}
=\sqrt{\frac{(6-7)^2+(7-7)^2+(8-7)^2+(10-7)^2+(4-7)^2}{5}}$\\
=$\sqrt{\frac{1^2+0^2+1^2+3^2+3^2}{5}}=\sqrt{\frac{20}{5}}=\sqrt{4}=$2
\end{gathered}

